<item><title>Mauritania raises pensions and public-sector pay from January</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-raises-pensions-and-public-sector-pay-from-afb743/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-raises-pensions-and-public-sector-pay-from-afb743/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>The changes include a monthly 10 000 old-ouguiya supplement for all civilian and military retirees, with a minimum pension of 50 000.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:25:11 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-raises-pensions-and-public-sector-pay-from-afb743/share.jpg" length="42615" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-raises-pensions-and-public-sector-pay-from-afb743/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mauritania allocated 305 million francs for independence celebrations</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-allocated-305-million-francs-for-independence-1c2ccc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-allocated-305-million-francs-for-independence-1c2ccc/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>A 1960 budget law drew on French aid and cancelled credits for government departments to finance the celebrations.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:35:32 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" length="34560" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mauritania joins OECD Development Centre</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-joins-oecd-development-centre-296656/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-joins-oecd-development-centre-296656/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>The membership was formalised at a high-level meeting in Paris as the government cited dialogue on development and international experience.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:18:59 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" length="34560" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Atar stages 5-kilometre cycling race for Independence anniversary</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/atar-stages-5-kilometre-cycling-race-for-independence-6b1c47/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/atar-stages-5-kilometre-cycling-race-for-independence-6b1c47/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>20 cyclists raced 5 kilometres in Atar on Friday, with the five leading finishers awarded prizes.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:54:48 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" length="34560" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Flaash Taxi lets Nouakchott riders see fares before booking</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/flaash-taxi-lets-nouakchott-riders-see-fares-before-booking-17d77c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/flaash-taxi-lets-nouakchott-riders-see-fares-before-booking-17d77c/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>Launched in September, the app detects a rider’s location and lets passengers pay in cash or from their Flaash account.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:54:01 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" length="34560" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
